  "question": {
    "text": "A value of $C$ for which the conclusion of Mean Value Theorem holds for the function $f(x)=$ $\\log _{\\mathrm{e}} x$ on the interval $[1,3]$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "exN9d",
      "text": "\n$2 \\log _3 e$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tftpT",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} \\log _{\\mathrm{e}} 3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OPLg0",
      "text": "\n$\\log _3 e$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ThPXH",
      "text": "\n$\\log _e 3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using mean value theorem\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& f^{\\prime}(c)=\\frac{f(3)-f(1)}{3-1} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{c}=\\frac{\\log 3-\\log 1}{2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow c=\\frac{2}{\\log _e 3}=2 \\log _3 e.\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
